PTLib 2.12-beta10 (OPAL stack): make the stack-size std::max unambiguous

PTHREAD_STACK_MIN is a long on glibc while stackSize is a PINDEX, so
std::max(stackSize, 16*PTHREAD_STACK_MIN) has two different deduced types and
does not compile.  Since glibc 2.34 PTHREAD_STACK_MIN is additionally not a
constant expression - it expands to sysconf(_SC_THREAD_STACK_MIN) - so the
mismatch cannot be resolved by the compiler folding it either.

The template argument is stated explicitly and the operand cast, which keeps the
selected value identical to what the original expression computed.

Applies to: 10503462abe31a6c288a39f6f894a5ceb367abbc (branch v2_12)
Upstream:   https://git.code.sf.net/p/opalvoip/ptlib

diff --git a/src/ptlib/unix/tlibthrd.cxx b/src/ptlib/unix/tlibthrd.cxx
index f436f8c..fec8a00 100644
--- a/src/ptlib/unix/tlibthrd.cxx
+++ b/src/ptlib/unix/tlibthrd.cxx
@@ -280,7 +280,7 @@ PThread::PThread(PINDEX stackSize,
                  Priority priorityLevel,
                  const PString & name)
   : m_type(deletion == AutoDeleteThread ? e_IsAutoDelete : e_IsManualDelete)
-  , m_originalStackSize(std::max(stackSize, 16*PTHREAD_STACK_MIN)) // Set a decent (256K) stack size that won't eat all virtual memory
+  , m_originalStackSize(std::max<PINDEX>(stackSize, (PINDEX)(16*PTHREAD_STACK_MIN))) // Set a decent (256K) stack size that won't eat all virtual memory
   , m_threadName(name)
   , m_threadId(PNullThreadIdentifier)  // indicates thread has not started
   , PX_priority(priorityLevel)
